---
const sandboxUrl = 'https://sandbox.textral.alacrity.ai';
const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/alacrity-ai/TextralAI';
---

<section class="py-20 md:py-28">
  <div class="container-default">
    <p
      class="text-center text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.04em] text-text-tertiary"
    >
      Deploy anywhere
    </p>
    <h2
      class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-3xl text-center font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-primary md:text-4xl"
    >
      Hosted, self-hosted, or both at once.
    </h2>
    <p
      class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-prose text-center text-lg text-text-secondary"
    >
      The MCP profile model lets one Claude Code session talk to a hosted
      dev instance and a self-hosted prod instance in the same
      conversation. We did not bolt this on as a v2 — it's how the product
      was built.
    </p>

    <figure class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl">
      <div
        class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-bg-elevated"
      >
        <img
          src="/brand/hosted-self-hosted-symmetry.png"
          alt="A mirrored architecture diagram with hosted Cloudflare deployment on the left and self-hosted infrastructure on the right, both connected through a shared @textral/contracts and @textral/sdk and @textral/mcp layer that produces identical outcomes."
          width="1254"
          height="1254"
          class="h-auto w-full"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article
        class="rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-bg-elevated p-8"
      >
        <p
          class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.04em] text-accent-teal"
        >
          Hosted
        </p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary">
          Hosted on Cloudflare
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base text-text-secondary">
          Spin up a tenant in the sandbox, get an API key, ingest your
          first document. We run the workers, the database, the vector
          store. You bring your provider keys (OpenAI, Anthropic, Voyage,
          Cohere) — or use ours.
        </p>
        <a
          href={sandboxUrl}
          class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-accent-teal hover:brightness-110"
        >
          Start in the sandbox
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </article>

      <article
        class="rounded-xl border border-border-subtle bg-bg-elevated p-8"
      >
        <p
          class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.04em] text-accent-coral"
        >
          Self-hosted
        </p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary">
          Self-hosted on your infra
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base text-text-secondary">
          Same packages. Same contracts. Deploy{' '}
          <code
            class="rounded-sm bg-bg-overlay px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-text-primary"
            >@textral/api</code
          >{' '}
          to your own Cloudflare account or your own runtime. The MCP
          server, SDKs, and audit trail work identically. No fork, no
          separate codebase to maintain.
        </p>
        <a
          href={`${repoUrl}#self-hosting`}
          rel="noopener"
          class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-accent-coral hover:brightness-110"
        >
          Self-hosting guide
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
